   "story": "The club approached him before the war ended, after he had turned down a job on Liverpool’s coaching staff because he wanted more responsibility for the playing side than merely selecting the team. After the Munich air disaster he rebuilt his side and won the FA Cup in 1963, two league titles in three years, and then the European Cup. He stayed one more year, handed the job to Wilf McGuinness, and returned for the second half of 1970–71 when McGuinness struggled."
