   "story": "Joined from Aberdeen on 6 November 1986, the day Ron Atkinson was sacked. Reportedly close to the sack himself, his first trophy at the club was the 1990 FA Cup, then the Cup Winners’ Cup in 1991 and the club’s first League Cup in 1992. In 1993 he won United’s first league title in 26 years, and in 1999 the Treble. His 13th and final league title in 2012–13 made it 20 for the club. He retired as the most decorated manager in football history."
